  "final_message": "I haven't made the change. As written, it conflicts with ARCH-4 in this repo's CLAUDE.md, so I need your call first.\n\n**The conflict:** `channel` is part of the published `OrderPlaced` event (`src/core/events.ts:16`, `schemaVersion: 3`). ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event from other repositories, and removing a field has to go through deprecation. Nothing in this repo reads `channel` except validation, but I can't see those two consumers or check what they read. If either one deserializes `channel` strictly, or analytics groups by it, dropping it without notice would break a deployed consumer.\n\nThe rest of the change is low risk:\n- The `GET /orders/{id}` response (`src/api/responses.ts`) doesn't include `channel`, so ARCH-8 isn't affected.\n- `POST /orders` accepts `channel` and checks it against `web | store | marketplace`. Removing it from the model means the request parser should accept the field and ignore it rather than reject it, so existing callers keep working.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Deprecate now, remove later (fits ARCH-4).** Mark `OrderPlaced.channel` `@deprecated` and keep publishing it. Make `channel` optional on `POST /orders` and stop requiring it in the core model. Remove the field from the event in a follow-up, once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it now.** Only if you've already confirmed with both consuming teams that they don't read `channel`, or Architecture has approved a breaking change. If so, tell me who confirmed and I'll note it in the commit. I'd also suggest bumping `schemaVersion` to 4.\n3. **Only remove it from the internal order model.** Stop storing or validating `channel` in the core, but keep the event field and fill it with a fixed or default value. This is usually the worst option, because consumers would get misleading data.\n\nI'd recommend option 1. Should I go ahead with it, or do you have consumer sign-off for option 2?",
